## 6. Validation ladder (each rung logged with commands and outputs)

1. static (`py_compile`, `bash -n`, `git diff --check`); 2. `pytest tests/` (all existing tests plus the new ones); 3. tiny synthetic forward with `--yaw-aug 1` (finite loss, gradients flow); 4. real-data readback on 50 batches: depth roll exact, source and reference distances unchanged, target and reference audio unchanged, **alignment audit** by `tools/yaw_aug.alignment_audit(batches, offsets, model)` (integer delays only, computed with the model's own `shift_and_align` on the GPU in float32 exactly as in training, for the rotated versus the un-rotated geometry; cohort = the first 50 micro-batches of epoch 1 with their counter offsets; artefact `alignment_audit.json` with the cohort digest (query paths + offsets), the changed-delay count and the denominator 12 800; reviewed with round 1); 5. smoke (exact argv, same environment and interpreter as the full run): `python train_xRIR_backbone.py --backbone simple --save-dir <attempt>/smoke --num-shot 8 --max-len 9600 --lr 1e-3 --weight-decay 1e-4 --decay-epochs 3 --lr-gamma 0.1 --epochs 1 --max-train-batches 3 --max-test-batches 2 --batch-size 4 --accum-steps 2 --num-workers 4 --seed 0 --tf32 --log-interval 1 --save-every 0 --epoch-ckpt-every 0 --no-save --yaw-aug 1 --yaw-aug-seed 0 --yaw-aug-width 512` (banner, three finite steps, nothing written); 6. throughput probe: 50 micro-batches at 32 × 2 with and without augmentation on the target GPU, overhead > 5 % blocks the launch; 7. parity audit: `--yaw-aug 0` loss on the first real batch equals the exp_01 script's loss bit for bit (same seed); type-strict diff of the launcher's pre-spawn `effective_args.json` against the control's `args.json`, excluding only `save_dir`, the three yaw keys, `no_save`, `PYTHONHASHSEED` and the cadence keys (`save_every`, `epoch_ckpt_every`), with every excluded difference listed in the notebook; 8. final integrative Codex review of the whole diff; 9. full run through a fail-closed launcher (`launch_yaw_aug.sh`: exact argv, source/data identity, empty output directory, free GPU and disk, banner flushed before step one, teed timestamped log).

## 7. Launch, acceptance criteria, monitoring

Full-run argv (exact, from the golden file): `XRIR_DATA_PATH=/home/yixunhu/data_cache/AcousticRooms PYTHONHASHSEED=0 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 /home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/bin/python train_xRIR_backbone.py --backbone simple --save-dir ckpt/xRIR_simple_yawaug_8_shot/attempt_<ts> --num-shot 8 --max-len 9600 --lr 1e-3 --weight-decay 1e-4 --decay-epochs 3 --lr-gamma 0.1 --epochs 12 --batch-size 32 --accum-steps 2 --num-workers 12 --seed 0 --tf32 --log-interval 50 --save-every 0 --epoch-ckpt-every 1 --yaw-aug 1 --yaw-aug-seed 0 --yaw-aug-width 512` (every trainer flag stated; the trainer's native checkpoint names are `epoch_001.pth` … `epoch_012.pth`; confirmatory: `epoch_012.pth`, diagnostic: `epoch_009.pth`). Written in `_worklog.md` before launch: commit SHA; GPU 0; the argv above; the banner in the log; ≥ 1 optimizer step with finite loss; **epoch-1 acceptance ≤ 2.431 h** (control's epoch 1 2.315 h + 5 %) with 2.6 h as a separate operational abort ceiling; `history.jsonl` one line per epoch; every `epoch_NNN.pth` present; no `--resume`. `_command.md` and `_params_set_up.md` at launch. Failure triage infrastructure vs bug; an interrupted attempt is preserved as `_ABORTED_` and a fresh attempt starts from epoch 1; **43 h is the cumulative ceiling over all attempts** — exceeding it requires renewed authorisation from the user.

## 8. Analysis and deliverables

`_results.md` generated from the producers' canonical JSON (paired_compare, results_table) — tables only; `_analysis.md` (Planner); `yaw_aug_xrir_01_results.html` + assets (reads producer JSON only, as exp_03); the table row values with their seed SD; `commits_yaw_aug_xrir.md`; provenance sidecars and binding for every new run as in exp_03.

## 9. Cost and risks

- Cost: ≈30 h training on GPU 0 (cumulative ceiling 43 h); ≈17 h of evaluation on GPU 1 (fresh five-seed comparators and the augmented arm's eight-angle blocks included); summaries minutes.
- Risks and limitations, stated now: (i) augmentation may raise the canonical-heading error on the axis-aligned test rooms (a finding under H1); (ii) one training seed per arm and non-shared training realizations (§2); (iii) the finite-precision alignment effect (§2 rule); (iv) throughput overhead (gated); (v) only the SimpleViT backbone is augmented.

## 10. Decisions requested from the user

1. Budget: 12 epochs (≈30 h) with the epoch-12 checkpoint as the only confirmatory comparison (recommended), the epoch-9 checkpoint reported as a diagnostic under the "40k" convention.
2. Only the SimpleViT backbone is augmented (no YawAug-CylindricalViT row; another ≈30 h if wanted).
3. Five evaluation seeds {42–46} for every table cell, including fresh re-evaluation of the control and the cylindrical checkpoints (≈4 h extra GPU) so the whole table shares one protocol.
4. Tests in `tests/`; the living table `worklog/worklog_yixun/model_comparison.md` introduced here.
5. R@1/5/10 stay undefined (no retrieval task exists in this pipeline).

## 11. v4 changelog (responses to the round-3 plan review)

